## What this project is, and what it derives from

capa-x is an independent reimplementation, in Rust, of the capability
detection performed by capa (https://github.com/mandiant/capa), which is
Copyright 2020 Google LLC and licensed under the Apache License 2.0. capa-x
is a *port*: its source files are original Rust, written against the pinned
Python capa source and the pinned Vivisect source as the behavioural
specification. It is not a translation of, and does not vendor, those code
bases.

The pinned upstream versions this port is written against are recorded in
PINNED.md.

### Statement of changes (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b))

capa-x does not reproduce upstream's results exactly. It is a new *backend*
for the capa rule format, and like capa's other backends it disagrees with the
Vivisect backend on some code-scope results. Every such difference measured on
the project's evaluation corpus is enumerated, with its root cause and the
upstream mechanism responsible, in KNOWN_DIVERGENCES.md. Users relying on
agreement with Python capa should read that file.

### Artifacts derived from capa

Two kinds of upstream material are redistributed in this repository rather
than reimplemented:

- `capa-x/sigs/*.sig` — FLIRT signature files copied verbatim from capa's
  `sigs/` directory. Per `capa-x/sigs/README.md` (also from capa), these
  were generated by Mandiant with the Hex-Rays FLAIR tools from source data
  Mandiant collected, are not derived from the FLIRT signatures distributed
  with IDA Pro, and carry the same Apache 2.0 license as capa.
- `capa-x/data/com_classes.json`, `capa-x/data/com_interfaces.json` —
  the COM class and interface GUID databases, extracted from capa's
  `capa/features/com/{classes,interfaces}.py` by `scripts/gen_com_db.py` and
  re-encoded as JSON. The data is capa's; only the encoding is this project's.

Beyond these, semantic constants ported from the Python source (string length
minimums, byte caps, window sizes, and similar) appear throughout
`capa-x/src/`, each with a comment naming the upstream file it came from.

### Behaviour ported from Vivisect

capa's default backend is built on Vivisect (https://github.com/vivisect/vivisect),
Copyright Vivisect contributors, licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
capa-x's code recovery reproduces Vivisect's codeflow behaviour — chiefly
  `capa-x/src/extract/recovery/recovery.rs` and `capa-x/src/extract/recovery/noreturn.rs`,
which are written against `vivisect/analysis/` and `vivisect/codeflow.py`.
Vivisect is not vendored here; it is a development-time dependency of the
difftest harness only, and capa-x has no Python at runtime.

### Submodules

The following are referenced as git submodules, pinned by commit. They are not
redistributed as part of this repository's own source, and each carries its own
license file:

- `rules/` — capa-rules (https://github.com/mandiant/capa-rules), Apache 2.0.
  Consumed unmodified; capa-x's purpose is to run these rules as written.
- `tests/testfiles/` — capa-testfiles
  (https://github.com/mandiant/capa-testfiles), Apache 2.0, Copyright (C) 2020
  Mandiant, Inc. Evaluation samples; used by the test suite and the difftest
  harness.
- `reference/capa/` — the pinned Python capa source, Apache 2.0. Present as the
  behavioural specification to read and to measure against, and never executed
  by capa-x itself.

